  "heads": [
    {
      "la": "QUARUM HAEC SUNT ARGUMENTA:",
      "column": "113c",
      "chunk": 0,
      "en": "OF WHICH THESE ARE THE ARGUMENTS:"
    },
    {
      "la": "PRAEFATIO. De varia sacrae Scripturae expositione, et de Salomonis intentione.",
      "column": "113c",
      "chunk": 0,
      "en": "PREFACE. On the varied exposition of Holy Scripture, and on Solomon's intention."
    },
    {
      "la": "HOMILIA PRIMA. De titulo operis, Salomonis nominibus, et libris, et principiis hujus operis, de vanitatum explanatione.",
      "column": "115c",
      "chunk": 1,
      "en": "HOMILY THE FIRST. On the title of the work, on Solomon's names, and books, and on the beginnings of this work, on the explanation of the vanities."
    },
    {
      "la": "HOMILIA II. De probatione vanitatis omnium sub coelo: per elementorum corruptionem, per rerum generationem, successionem, et eorum, quae fuerunt oblivionem.",
      "column": "133b",
      "chunk": 7,
      "en": "HOMILY II. On the proof of the vanity of all things under heaven: through the corruption of the elements, through the generation of things, the succession, and the forgetting of those things which have been."
    },
    {
      "la": "HOMILIA III. Quomodo Ecclesiastes probet per sua opera omnia hominum opera vana, cum praedictorum epilogo.",
      "column": "149d",
      "chunk": 13,
      "en": "HOMILY III. How Ecclesiastes proves through his own works that all the works of men are vain, with an epilogue of the things aforesaid."
    },
    {
      "la": "HOMILIA IV. De rerum vanitate, et hominum occupatione pessima.",
      "column": "151c",
      "chunk": 14,
      "en": "HOMILY IV. On the vanity of things, and the worst occupation of men."
    },
    {
      "la": "HOMILIA V. De dictorum verborum Ecclesiastae litterali et morali expositione.",
      "column": "153c",
      "chunk": 15,
      "en": "HOMILY V. On the literal and moral exposition of the words of Ecclesiastes already spoken."
    },
    {
      "la": "HOMILIA VI. Quid sit distendi in occupatione pessima.",
      "column": "157c",
      "chunk": 17,
      "en": "HOMILY VI. What it is to be distended in the worst occupation."
    },
    {
      "la": "HOMILIA VII. Quod perversi difficile corrigantur, etc.",
      "column": "159b",
      "chunk": 18,
      "en": "HOMILY VII. That the perverse are corrected with difficulty, etc."
    },
    {
      "la": "HOMILIA VIII. Quod homo a veritate aufugit: ut Adam in paradiso fugit, et abscondit se.",
      "column": "164c",
      "chunk": 20,
      "en": "HOMILY VIII. That man flees away from the truth: as Adam in paradise fled, and hid himself."
    },
    {
      "la": "HOMILIA IX. De diversis vanis Ecclesiastae conatibus.",
      "column": "169d",
      "chunk": 22,
      "en": "HOMILY IX. On the various vain endeavors of Ecclesiastes."
    },
    {
      "la": "HOMILIA X. De reliquis vanitatibus usque in eum locum: « Stultus in tenebris ambulat. »",
      "column": "172b",
      "chunk": 23,
      "en": "HOMILY X. On the remaining vanities, as far as that place: « The fool walketh in darkness. »"
    },
    {
      "la": "HOMILIA XI. Qui sint fines terrae in quibus sunt oculi stultorum: et quomodo sapientia attingit a fine usque ad finem fortiter, etc.",
      "column": "182d",
      "chunk": 27,
      "en": "HOMILY XI. What the ends of the earth are in which the eyes of fools are: and how wisdom reacheth from end to end mightily, etc."
